WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.680
Welcome to DBL Group’s TalentHub!
Does your unit need additional manpower?

2
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.520
In this video, we’ll see how to create
a requisition, what happens after

3
00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:17.280
submission, and how to make corrections
if it’s returned. Let’s get started!

4
00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.910
In TalentHub,
you’ll see the relevant menus

5
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:26.190
and features based on your assigned
access. Let’s begin by signing in.

6
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.860
Enter your official DBL
Group email and password.

7
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:35.140
If you’re using your own computer,
you can select Remember

8
00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:41.340
me to have your email appear automatically
next time. Now click Sign in.

9
00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:47.210
The previous paper-based Employee
Requisition Form is now fully digital in

10
00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:52.130
TalentHub. You can easily create
requisitions for new manpower by

11
00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.210
providing the required position details

12
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.170
and specifying the applicable
facilities for the new employee.

13
00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.880
The sidebar contains Dashboard,
Requisitions, Organogram,

14
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.920
Employees, and Notifications. Most of
your work will be done under Requisitions.

15
00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:14.430
Now let’s create a new requisition.
The form has two steps: position details,

16
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.070
followed by Facility Requirements
for the new employee.

17
00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:22.710
Start by clicking Requisitions.

18
00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.910
The tiles at the top show the number of
requisitions under different statuses,

19
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:31.660
with the complete list below.

20
00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:36.500
To create a new requisition,
click New requisition on the right.

21
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.530
Notice that Raising as
already displays your name,

22
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.290
while Unit / Factory
shows your assigned unit.

23
00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.810
If you have access to multiple units,
select the appropriate one.

24
00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:50.130
Then choose the Line of Business.

25
00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.800
Under Department, select the
department that requires manpower.

26
00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.320
For this example,
we’re selecting Plant HR.

27
00:01:59.839 --> 00:02:03.360
If there’s a specific Section,
select that as well.

28
00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:08.310
Under Designation or Job title,
select the position.

29
00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:11.699
For this example,
we’re choosing Executive.

30
00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:15.990
If you also want to consider candidates
at Officer or Senior Officer level,

31
00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:20.270
use Add another designation to
include additional positions.

32
00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.660
Under Requisition type, select the
reason for the manpower requirement.

33
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:31.380
Choose New for a newly created position or
Replace when hiring a replacement for an

34
00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:35.170
existing employee. In this example,
we’re selecting Replace.

35
00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:40.397
In the Employee field,
select the employee being replaced.

36
00:02:40.517 --> 00:02:44.290
For this example,
we’re selecting Sadia Islam.

37
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:50.491
Next, specify the reason for leaving,
such as Better Opportunity.

38
00:02:50.611 --> 00:02:55.530
If you’re replacing multiple employees,
use Add another employee.

39
00:02:55.880 --> 00:03:00.000
Under Nos. of required post,
enter the number of employees required.

40
00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:05.520
For this example, we’re entering one.
The Total no. of vacant

41
00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.720
post field automatically displays the
available vacancies from the organogram.

42
00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:13.310
Under Place of posting,
select the workplace.

43
00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:17.310
For this example,
we’re choosing Jinnat Complex.

44
00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.590
Next, enter the date the
position became vacant

45
00:03:20.710 --> 00:03:25.990
and the date by which the
new employee is needed.

46
00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:31.780
Under Priority, select how
urgently the manpower is required.

47
00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:36.948
For this example, we’re choosing Moderate.
Then select the employment type:

48
00:03:37.068 --> 00:03:42.820
Permanent, Temporary,
or Contractual. Now click Next.

49
00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:46.010
Now let’s move to Step 2,
Facility Requirements.

50
00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:51.530
Select the facilities
required for the new employee.

51
00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:56.090
If a laptop or desktop is needed,
select Needed and choose the device type.

52
00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:01.170
For this example, we’re selecting Laptop.

53
00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.880
Keep in mind that selecting Transport

54
00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:09.120
or Dormitory does not
guarantee these facilities.

55
00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:13.720
Transport depends on routes,
schedules, and seat availability,

56
00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.720
while Dormitory depends on available
accommodation and allocation.

57
00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.690
The conditions are mentioned in the form.

58
00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.350
Finally, under Seating Arrangement,

59
00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:28.070
select Needed if seating is required.

60
00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:32.430
Then specify whether an existing seat
will be used or a new one is needed.

61
00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:36.070
For this example,
we’re selecting Existing seat.

62
00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:40.990
Review all the details
and click Send for job analysis.

63
00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.500
Your requisition has been
created successfully,

64
00:04:45.020 --> 00:04:48.660
and the system has automatically
generated a Requisition Number.

65
00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.620
The current status is Job Analysis,
meaning the

66
00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:58.436
requisition has been forwarded to Factory
HR, and they’ve received a notification.

67
00:04:58.786 --> 00:05:03.626
After submission,
the requisition first goes to Factory HR.

68
00:05:03.746 --> 00:05:06.394
They complete Section B
with the Job Description,

69
00:05:06.514 --> 00:05:10.026
Qualifications,
and Experience requirements,

70
00:05:10.146 --> 00:05:12.986
and attach the detailed JD.

71
00:05:13.106 --> 00:05:16.274
The requisition
then moves to the Approval Process.

72
00:05:16.624 --> 00:05:22.824
Next, the Approval Process begins. Under
the Approvals tab, you can see who needs

73
00:05:22.944 --> 00:05:28.824
to approve, who has already approved,
when they approved, and any comments.

74
00:05:29.024 --> 00:05:33.584
The requisition moves through each
approver in the predefined sequence.

75
00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:38.987
The Approval Chain is determined
when the requisition is created.

76
00:05:39.107 --> 00:05:42.533
Even if Approval Paths are updated later,

77
00:05:42.653 --> 00:05:46.014
the Approval Chain of an existing
requisition remains unchanged.

78
00:05:46.364 --> 00:05:49.524
Let’s understand the requisition statuses.

79
00:05:49.644 --> 00:05:54.164
Job Analysis means Factory HR is
preparing the position details.

80
00:05:54.844 --> 00:05:59.044
Pending Approval means the
approval process is ongoing.

81
00:05:59.164 --> 00:06:02.537
Approved means all approvals are complete.

82
00:06:02.657 --> 00:06:06.884
Profile Ready means the Role
Profile has been created.

83
00:06:07.004 --> 00:06:11.364
Posted means the vacancy has been
published on the Career Page.

84
00:06:11.484 --> 00:06:15.216
Rejected means the
requisition was not approved.

85
00:06:15.566 --> 00:06:20.086
A requisition may be returned
to you in two situations.

86
00:06:20.206 --> 00:06:25.446
First, when Factory HR requests
additional information or corrections.

87
00:06:25.566 --> 00:06:28.166
You’ll receive a notification.

88
00:06:29.006 --> 00:06:32.046
Click the Bell icon at the
top to view the details.

89
00:06:32.396 --> 00:06:37.636
In the Job Analysis tab, Factory HR’s
comments will explain which information

90
00:06:37.756 --> 00:06:43.676
needs correction. The requisition status
remains Job Analysis during this process.

91
00:06:44.026 --> 00:06:47.426
Click Edit details to make
the required corrections.

92
00:06:47.546 --> 00:06:51.006
For this example,
we’re changing the Vacant date.

93
00:06:51.126 --> 00:06:54.986
Once the changes are complete,
click Save changes.

94
00:06:55.336 --> 00:06:58.656
Now click Resend for job analysis.

95
00:06:59.096 --> 00:07:03.096
The requisition will be
forwarded back to Factory HR.

96
00:07:03.446 --> 00:07:09.566
The second situation occurs when an
approver requests additional information

97
00:07:09.686 --> 00:07:14.206
during the approval process.
If they select Need more info,

98
00:07:14.326 --> 00:07:19.485
the approval process pauses and the
requisition returns to you. You can view

99
00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:23.846
their comments under Sent back to you
for clarification in the Approvals tab.

100
00:07:24.196 --> 00:07:27.756
If necessary, update the
information through Edit details.

101
00:07:27.956 --> 00:07:30.876
Then click Send for approval.

102
00:07:31.156 --> 00:07:34.236
The requisition will re-enter
the approval process,

103
00:07:34.356 --> 00:07:37.156
and the Approval Chain will
restart from the first level.

104
00:07:37.506 --> 00:07:42.346
If a requisition is rejected, you can
view the reason in the Approvals tab.

105
00:07:42.626 --> 00:07:48.665
If required, you may create a new
requisition. To request cancellation of an

106
00:07:48.785 --> 00:07:52.946
already submitted requisition,
contact the responsible person.

107
00:07:53.296 --> 00:07:57.656
Once all approvers have approved, the
requisition status changes to Approved.

108
00:07:58.496 --> 00:08:02.696
The Head of Talent Acquisition
then determines the CV sources

109
00:08:02.816 --> 00:08:06.056
and assigns a Corporate Recruiter,

110
00:08:06.816 --> 00:08:11.496
who manages the recruitment
process through onboarding.

111
00:08:12.416 --> 00:08:16.576
You’ll receive important
updates through notifications.

112
00:08:16.926 --> 00:08:18.726
Here’s a useful tip.

113
00:08:18.846 --> 00:08:23.766
Before creating a requisition,
you can check the approved positions

114
00:08:23.886 --> 00:08:26.806
and vacancies in the Organogram.

115
00:08:26.926 --> 00:08:31.246
This helps you understand the current
manpower situation in your unit.

116
00:08:31.596 --> 00:08:36.196
Whenever there’s an update to your
requisition, a notification appears under

117
00:08:36.316 --> 00:08:40.266
the Bell icon, accompanied by a short
sound and an on-screen message. The system

118
00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:44.996
updates automatically, so there’s no need
to refresh repeatedly. Open Notifications

119
00:08:45.116 --> 00:08:50.956
to view all updates. Important
notifications are also sent by email.

120
00:08:51.306 --> 00:08:56.227
If you’d like to disable email
notifications, go to the Notifications tab

121
00:08:56.506 --> 00:09:00.266
under Settings and turn off
the Email notifications option.

122
00:09:00.616 --> 00:09:03.696
Let’s answer a few common questions.

123
00:09:03.816 --> 00:09:07.536
Can’t find your unit in
the Unit / Factory list,

124
00:09:07.656 --> 00:09:13.776
or seeing Approval path not found?

125
00:09:13.896 --> 00:09:17.496
Contact Factory HR or the Head of
Talent Acquisition for assistance.

126
00:09:17.846 --> 00:09:23.086
As a Requisition Raiser, you don’t
have direct access to candidates’ CVs.

127
00:09:23.206 --> 00:09:26.846
However, if you’re invited
to an Interview Panel,

128
00:09:26.966 --> 00:09:30.486
you can view the relevant interview
details under My Interviews.

129
00:09:30.836 --> 00:09:35.356
The complete guide for this process
is available as a PDF under Tutorials.

130
00:09:36.356 --> 00:09:39.676
For system access issues,

131
00:09:39.796 --> 00:09:43.516
contact Factory HR
or the Head of Talent Acquisition.

132
00:09:44.396 --> 00:09:48.476
For login-related issues,
contact the IT Helpdesk.

133
00:09:49.476 --> 00:09:52.676
Thank you for using DBL Group’s TalentHub.

